# The SAME payload, version and keys as sample-v3.rlxu.hex, declared for
# flash destination 0x030000 in `whole` form -- so the two differ in
# bytes 64..71 and in the 64 signature bytes and NOWHERE else.  That is
# the committed proof that the destination and the landing form are
# inside what is signed; in format 1 the two builds had the same
# sha256.  A7 rebuilds it byte for byte and A8 verifies it; N4 drives
# it against --write-at/--write-form in both directions.

